    "description": "ASKUL Corporation engages in e-commerce business in Japan. It operates through the E-Commerce Business and Logistics Business segments. The company operates ASKUL, an e-commerce website for businesses where customers can shop for various products, such as office supplies, office living supplies, office furniture, and specialized goods for the manufacturing and construction sectors; general medical products for the healthcare, nursing care, and drugstore industries; medicinal materials, including pharmaceuticals and medical equipment; and food products, alcoholic beverages, and cosmetics. It also provides enterprise procurement solutions; Papuri, a specialized service to make printed materials, such as business cards, envelopes, stamps, and personalized novelty goods; office coordinate services for office interior layouts; and an e-commerce website of professional items for dentists. In addition, the company engages in the sale of maintenance, repair, and operation supplies; provision of facility management services and purchase solutions for large companies; and agent business activities. Further, it is involved in the operation of e-commerce sites for pet and gardening products; provision of logistics and small-cargo transportation, product storage, warehouse management, and delivery services for manufacturers and direct-order companies; and production and sale of bottled natural mineral water. ASKUL Corporation was incorporated in 1963 and is headquartered in Koto, Japan."
